1
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:45,200
Respected Muslims!

2
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:54,780
The Messenger of God, who appeared with a universal invitation,

3
00:00:55,980 --> 00:01:03,120
is an exceptional and distinguished person whom all beings ranging from fish to the angels,

4
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:07,000
from djinns to the humans listen to and are all ears

5
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:13,220
when he speaks and regard him as the sultan of oratory.

6
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:20,580
In the congregation of the Prayers the Messenger of God, peace, and blessings be upon him, led,

7
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:25,480
there were many creatures that range from djinns to humans,

8
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:33,180
from humans to angels, from angels to spiritual creatures and fish.

9
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:41,160
Creatures from Heavens, Earth, and Kursi attended the Prayers of the Messenger of God,

10
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,960
said amen to that beloved servant of God's prayers,

11
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:50,500
and wished and requested for the same things he wished from God.

12
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,680
The Honorable Prophet Muhammad, peace, and blessings be upon him,

13
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:05,240
gathered all the creatures behind him with his Khutbahs that he gave and made them be all ears.

14
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,600
Whether humans realized this or not,

15
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:15,520
even in the realms where he (the Messenger of God or humans in general) was not aware of it,

16
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:22,940
there have been awakenings and waving, eavesdropping on what he said,

17
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:28,180
hearts have started to overflow with excitement for him, and all of a sudden,

18
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:32,820
only the Khutbah of him, peace, and blessings be upon him, became audible.

19
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:39,700
It became audible that the mysterious events in the sky

20
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:45,680
and the earth prompted Djinns to seek him on earth.

21
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,860
They were wandering around.

22
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:54,680
Village by village, town by town, they were greeting and looking for him.

23
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:57,960
There was someone playing with the skies.

24
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:01,540
There was a person who established a relationship between the sky and the earth,

25
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:09,360
who came with the solution for the great mystery and enigma.

26
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,500
They were on their way up to Mecca.

27
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:22,040
They found the individual, who had the keys to the mysteries,

28
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:26,300
in the mosque built for the sake of him today.

29
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:29,360
The Messenger of God was reciting the Qur'an.

30
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:33,760
A handful of his companions had gathered around him.

31
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:39,820
Let's say two or three or four or five, but let him (the Honorable Prophet) not be sad...

32
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,420
The Djinns looked for and found him

33
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:46,800
and angles were all ears to what he was saying.

34
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:53,680
The Messenger of God was reciting the Qur'an. God had directed Djinns.

35
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:59,680
"We directed a company of jinn towards you in order

36
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:05,120
that they might listen to the Qur'an " conveys God.

37
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:08,400
We directed them.

38
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:15,520
We drove them around, took them to Mecca.

39
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:20,420
"When they were present for it",

40
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:26,080
they stood in reverence with the understanding of servitude.

41
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:30,880
"They said (to one another): 'Be silent and listen!'

42
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:36,200
It does not sound like any other word.

43
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:41,860
Be silent and listen! Here is the solver of problems.

44
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:47,560
Be silent so that we absorb the Qur'an. Here, it comes the solver of mysteries.

45
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:54,440
"Be all ears, be all ears!" they said. They were silent and eavesdropped.

46
00:04:54,780 --> 00:04:59,260
While listening to the Messenger of God there, they were overwhelmed with excitement.

47
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:03,420
There were calls of "be all ears" among them.

48
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:08,220
The truthful Messenger of God heard these voices and overflowed with exuberance.

49
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:19,600
"When the recitation finished, they returned to their community as warners.

50
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:24,460
They said: 'O our people! We have listened to a Book which has been sent after Moses,

51
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:29,960
confirming (the Divine origin of and the truths that are still contained by) the Revelations prior to it:

52
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:42,660
it guides towards the truth and towards a straight road (in all matters)."

53
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:46,700
As I understand (as opposed to mufassirs),

54
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:52,640
those djinns that came were probably Jewish that believed in the Honorable Moses.

55
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:07,480
We have listened to a Book which has been sent after Moses, confirming the Revelations prior to it:

56
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:13,020
it guides towards the truth and towards a straight road (in all matters).

57
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:24,960
O our people! Respond to him who calls to God, and believe in him.

58
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:28,100
God will forgive you your sins and save you from a painful punishment

59
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,120
O our people!  Listen to this voice.

60
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:35,620
O our people! Try to find your consistency and shape in the Qur'an.

61
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:40,880
According to hadiths narrated by Ibn Masud, Anas, Muaz, and Abu Dharr,

62
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:46,740
people were coming in throngs to the Messenger of God.

63
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:52,880
The Messenger of God would go in the future, teach them (Djinns) the law of religion,

64
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:58,160
teach the rules about what they eat and drink,

65
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:02,160
and the law of haram and halal.

66
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:06,400
He would accept their invitation and visit them, explain everything to them

67
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:14,260
and upon returning from there, tell us that

68
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:22,400
he recited the Surah of Ar-Rahman to all Djinn.

69
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:27,760
In Surah of Ar-Rahman, Djinns and humans are depicted together.

70
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:31,920
The order and system of the skies and the earth are explained.

71
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:35,920
The balance laid down by God is explained.

72
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:39,120
Rules and laws of God are explained.

73
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:43,140
Nature and natural conditions are explained.

74
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:48,980
Ruler of all these things is told. It is told that everything is in the power of that Ruler.

75
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:52,840
Then the creation of Djinns and humans are explained.

76
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:12,700
"Then (O humankind and jinn), which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?"

77
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:18,340
East and West are told within the borders where everyone (different kinds of creatures) lives.

78
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:27,540
He is the Lord of the two easts, and the Lord of the two wests.

79
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:37,080
He (God) introduces Himself as “the Lord of the points of sunrise and sunset".

80
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:40,880
Then (O humankind and jinn), which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?

81
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:45,220
Seas, pearl in those seas are told.

82
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:48,480
Then (O humankind and jinn), which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?

83
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:52,600
The seas, the ships in the seas, the kingdom to be established...

84
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:55,940
Then (O humankind and jinn), which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?

85
00:08:56,280 --> 00:09:03,800
Finally, the mortal world... the world is going to complete its lifetime... the sun is going to wane... the things and events are going to disappear...

86
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:14,140
You are going to enter His presence and enjoy His grace and blessings.

87
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:20,940
For this, the world and all mortal things must complete their lifespan...

88
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:25,720
Then (O humankind and jinn), which of the favors of your Lord will you deny even in the face of this blessing?

89
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:32,180
All those from the skies and the earth are going to be questioned;

90
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:36,700
everyone is going to account for their deeds and then balances of absolute justice

91
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:40,280
on the Day of Resurrection are going to be set up...

92
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:43,600
All these are conveyed respectively to Djinns and humans.

93
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:47,020
The Hell is described with all its fearsomeness.

94
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,900
Heaven is described with all its heartwarming blessings.

95
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:55,560
It is described with its houris and gilmans, untouched by any Djinn and human.

96
00:09:56,760 --> 00:10:03,660
Finally, it ends with "Blessed and Supreme is the Name of your Lord, the One of Majesty and Munificence!"

97
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:09,800
His Lord Almighty and His Holiness

98
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:15,780
His holy way of executing all these things.

99
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:20,480
Surah of Ar-Rahman lifted Djinns' spirit so much so

100
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:24,980
that after the Messenger of God returned,

101
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:29,760
he read it to his companions, but he did not like their attitude and said:

102
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:52,280
"Djinn were giving a better response than you are.

103
00:10:55,980 --> 00:11:00,360
Whenever I recited 'then (O humankind and jinn), which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?’

104
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:04,260
they winced and said: 'No, O, our Lord!

105
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:09,260
We do not deny any of your blessings. All praise and gratitude are for you.'”

106
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:13,320
Companions of the Messenger of God did not reply well.

107
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:20,160
The Messenger of God was pointing out this.

108
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:53,400
Verses of God were being recited to the community of Djinns.

109
00:11:54,400 --> 00:12:00,380
Djinns bent their necks, surrendered to what was recited, and encircled around the Messenger of God.

110
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:06,220
From that century onwards, the Qur'an translates the same truths

111
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:08,740
and expresses the same things.

112
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:11,220
What happened to your heart?

113
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,060
What happened to your soul?

114
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:18,980
What happened, even though the divine blessings are raining down on your head,

115
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:24,020
what happened that even though God keeps pouring down His blessings,

116
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:31,160
you are so sluggish towards the divine blessings?

117
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,180
When will you say (so)?

118
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:46,160
When will you make the Qur'an your life's pillar and say that 'we do not deny anything'?

119
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:51,020
When will you adhere to all orders and edicts (of your Lord)?

120
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:55,180
When will you make it (Qur'an) the principle of your life?

121
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:03,520
When will you stop pretending to live and truly claim Qur'an under the dome of it?

122
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:09,040
When will your nights be brighter than your days?

123
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:14,020
When will you go on the path of enlightening your grave?

124
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:19,220
When will you become the people of Darussalam (one of the layers of Jannah - Paradise in Islam)?

125
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:22,800
When will you understand God's purposes?

126
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:27,860
When will you listen to Qur'an as if you are listening to it from the Honorable Muhammad?

127
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:34,100
And when will you get rid of three-centuries of heedlessness

128
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:38,360
and believe in God again, as Ibn Rawaha puts it?

129
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:42,420
O you who believe! When will you believe in God?

130
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:46,880
God conveys in His Qur'an:

131
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:50,200
"O you who believe! Believe in God."

132
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:54,460
O those who pretend to do so! Believe in God in the real sense.

133
00:13:54,760 --> 00:14:00,120
O those who roam on the borders (of faith)! Be involved as the Companions of Badr (Battle of Badr).

134
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:05,380
O those who spend their nights in cozy and soft beds!

135
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:10,240
O those who spend days in carelessness! Believe in God.

136
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,780
When will you believe in God?

137
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:19,900
When will you hear the call and say, "We have indeed heard a wonderful Qur'an"?

138
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:26,160
When will the waves of the Qur'an bring the excitement of faith in you?

139
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:31,900
When will sins and wrongdoings say goodbye and get away from your streets and market places?

140
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:36,180
When will a world be established where we will not see any lie?

141
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:41,420
When will a perfect order in which bribery is not present will be established?

142
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:45,440
When will your head of state become dignified

143
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:49,720
and your parliamentarians will become truthful individuals?

144
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:57,580
When will you have the conditions to tell the truth without hesitation and being frightened in front of them?

145
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:03,020
When will you be free from being humiliated in the face of interests unlike the Pharaohs?

146
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:06,620
When will you take a stand against dangers and harmful things?

147
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:09,600
When will you say that enough is enough for us to lie down and sit,

148
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:13,200
let's go from village to village town to town (to tell our cause to people)?

149
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:19,180
When will you stop being away from the Qur'an even though you are in mosques?

150
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:25,820
When will you leave the devious path and heresy while you are in a valley and the Qur'an in a separate valley?

151
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,840
When will you take down the Qur'an from the shelves and descend into it?

152
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:36,100
When will you remove the mold, rust of the Qur’an, and claim it as your book?

153
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:39,100
O, People! When?

154
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:44,820
When will you say, "We have indeed heard a wonderful Qur'an" wherever you go?

155
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:48,700
When will you say, "I accept the Inviter of God (the Messenger of God)"?

156
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:52,080
Respond to God's Inviter!

157
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:55,740
Embark on this path!

158
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:59,820
Do not take your head off the threshold of the Messenger of God!

159
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:02,960
May the promised dawn break...

160
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,440
May his voice sing sweetly.

161
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:12,220
May the spirit of the Honorable Muhammad be represented and emerge on your horizon.

162
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:15,280
May your heart be calm and confident.

163
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:21,960
May God be pleased with you. May He enable you to perpetuate and be stable on His true path...